target.description:
`"all"`, a view id or a breakpoint id; when absent the views the flow names in its `//
@views` comment, else all. Also `"visible"` (the views the grid shows) or a list of view ids
and breakpoint ids.

position.description:
`left`, `right` or `bottom` docks the panels there; `floating` puts them in a window of
their own; `closed` closes them (to the icon rail, or hidden, as `panels.closeTo` says);
`hidden` hides them.

states.description:
The states the element gets, replacing what it had: `hover`, `active`, `focus`,
`focus-visible`, `focus-within`, `visited`, `target` (with or without the colon);
`["hover"]` when absent, `[]` takes the element's states back.
